{"operations":[{"content":"def is_valid(number: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if the provided number string is valid per the Luhn algorithm.\"\"\"\n    # Remove spaces\n    number = number.replace(' ', '')\n    if not number.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    total = 0\n    # Process digits from right to left\n    digits = list(map(int, number))\n    # The check digit is the last digit (rightmost), which is never doubled\n    # Double every second digit from the right, starting from the digit before the check digit\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1, -1, -1):\n        digit = digits[i]\n        # Determine if this digit should be doubled\n        # Positions counted from right: index from right = len(digits) - 1 - i\n        # Double if index from right is odd (1,3,5,...), i.e. every second digit from right excluding check digit\n        if (len(digits) - 1 - i) % 2 == 1:\n            digit *= 2\n            if digit > 9:\n                digit -= 9\n        total += digit\n\n    return total % 10 == 0\n","expected_sha256":"daa56df7794aa8b4da213da4d9fdee84518147a03a7f4ee745a11a06b101c3b1","kind":"modify","path":"src/luhn.py"}],"rationale":"Corrected the doubling logic in is_valid to double every second digit from the right excluding the check digit, per the Luhn algorithm specification. This fixes the defect so that '4539 1488 0343 6467' is valid and '4539 1488 0343 6468' is invalid, while keeping the public API and existing tests unchanged."}